::: {.callout-tip}
## The one-SE rule

A common heuristic: instead of picking the model with the lowest CV score, pick the simplest model
whose score is within one standard error of the best. This guards against overfitting to the
validation folds and tends to produce more parsimonious models.
:::

You can now use K-fold cross-validation to compare models, select basis dimensions, and apply the
one-SE rule for parsimonious model selection.

